{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_1","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc 'cat collab/1790489440000-vm-engineer-dao-stream-remote-slice3-fixes.glm-flash.report.md'","aggregated_output":"All three gate findings fixed in the three permitted files only (`src/cljc/dao/stream/ws_project.cljc`, `test/dao/stream/ws_project_test.cljc`, `test/dao/stream/ws_project_jvm_test.clj`); nothing committed/staged; gate-confirmed behavior preserved; added/edited lines are pure ASCII and <= 80 cols; cljstyle check clean and clj-kondo 0 errors / 0 warnings on all three files; no diagnostics left behind (the pre-existing comments-only `M src/cljc/dao/stream/ws.cljc` was untouched by me).\n\n**P1 — ring left open when the traffic medium ends.** `step!`'s `:dao.stream/end` case now closes the ring before marking the projection closed (`ws_project.cljc:117-119`); the ns and `step!` docstrings state the new reading (`ws_project.cljc:11-16`, `:96-102`). Tests: the rejected minimal-reading test was rewritten as `the-mediums-own-end-closes-the-projection-and-the-ring` (`ws_project_test.cljc:257` — retained values still forward, ring reads `end`, never a blocked wait), and the gate's link test `the-mediums-end-is-channel-loss-for-the-link` (`ws_project_test.cljc:272`) drives a real `dial`/`dial-attach!`/`dial-step!` composition whose link answers `transport-error` with `:dao.stream.remote/channel-gone` after the medium ends.\n\n**P1 — closed sessions accumulate in `:sessions`.** New private `reaped` (`ws_project.cljc:235-245`) drops sessions whose projection closed; `accept-step!` applies it after the per-session projection+mirror loop (`ws_project.cljc:277`), so the tick's mirror pass — the closed ring's last, which answers what its retained requests can still be answered — runs before removal; `accept-step!` and `session-end` docstrings updated (`:247-258`, `:288-295`). Tests: portable `a-closed-session-is-reaped-and-its-slot-is-reused` (`ws_project_test.cljc:377`) over a real `ws/make-endpoint` — the retained request is answered in the reap tick and a second connection is adopted and projects onto its own fresh ring; JVM real-socket `a-reaped-session-lets-the-next-connection-serve` (`ws_project_jvm_test.clj:373`) — close, reap, then a second connection over the same listener/endpoint/traffic medium reads \"hello\" again with exactly one session and the first's state gone. The existing `a-closed-connection-is-the-links-end` pred was adjusted to the reaping reality (`ws_project_jvm_test.clj:319-331`); its link assertions are unchanged.\n\n**P2 — second `dial-attach!` silently replaced the channel.** Chose the minimal reading: reject. A dial that already attached throws a composition error (`ws_project.cljc:364-368`) before any ws attach runs — the ring and traffic cursor already belong to the first attachment, and reuse would mix two attachments' state; documented in `dial-attach!`'s docstring (`:348-361`), consistent with `dial`'s existing \"one active attachment; a reattachment composes a fresh dial with a fresh cursor\". Test: `a-second-attach-on-one-dial-is-a-composition-error` (`ws_project_test.cljc:292`, portable `thrown?` across all three lanes); the JVM slot-reuse test exercises the documented reattachment path via a fresh dial + fresh cursor.\n\n**Lane counts (sequential, solo, via mise):**\n- JVM `mise exec -- clj -M:test`: **2,272 tests / 183,324 assertions / 0 failures, 0 errors** (baseline 2,268/183,303; +4 tests = 3 portable + 1 JVM)\n- Node `mise exec -- bb test:cljs`: **2,180 tests / 49,877 assertions / 0 failures, 0 errors** (baseline 2,177/49,865)\n- Dart `mise exec -- bb test:cljd`: **2,142 passed, All tests passed!** (baseline 2,139)\n\nStatus: COMPLETE","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
