)))))))\n   183\t\n   184\t\n   185\t(defn mirror-step\n   186\t  \"The pure step a peer runs over a channel to answer requests against\n   187\t   its table: `(mirror-step table chan-reader cursor chan-writer) ->\n   188\t   cursor'`. For each request read from chan-reader at `cursor`, in\n   189\t   order, the four steps of 2.3 run; the mirror holds no state between\n   190\t   calls beyond the returned cursor. A value that is neither a\n   191\t   well-formed request nor a well-formed answer is dropped as malformed\n   192\t   wire input. The step stops when the channel reader answers blocked\n   193\t   or end; a gap adopts the reader's own recovery cursor, the lost wire\n   194\t   values being lost. The mirror never constructs, parses or rewrites\n   195\t   a cursor, an anchor or an outcome: the served stream is the\n   196\t   original, its cursors, its positions, its gap, its end.\"\n   197\t  [table chan-reader cursor chan-writer]\n   198\t  (let [channel (:dao.stream/identity (stream/descriptor chan-reader))]\n   199\t    (loop [cursor cursor]\n   200\t      (let [r (stream/next chan-reader cursor)]\n   201\t        (case (:dao.stream/outcome r)\n   202\t          :dao.stream/ok\n   203\t          (do (when (well-formed-request? (:dao.stream/value r))\n   204\t                (answer! table chan-writer channel\n   205\t                         (:dao.stream/value r)))\n   206\t              (recur (:dao.stream/cursor r)))\n   207\t          :dao.stream/blocked cursor\n   208\t          :dao.stream/end cursor\n   209\t          :dao.stream/gap (recur (:dao.stream/cursor r))\n   210\t          cursor)))))\n   211\t\n   212\t\n   213\t;; =============================================================================\n   214\t;; The link (2.4, 2.5)\n   215\t;; =============================================================================\n   216\t\n   217\t(defn- new-link\n   218\t  \"One link per channel descriptor, shared by every reflection through\n   219\t   that channel. A link holds the channel writer; the channel reader\n   220\t   and the link's own cursor on it; the outstanding request ids with\n   221\t   the request each was sent for; the attach descriptor probes the\n   222\t   writer has refused, kept unsent with the reflection each was sent\n   223\t   for; filed answers keyed by id; the more outcomes installed at\n   224\t   their served identity and the cursor that precedes each; an\n   225\t   optional event writer; and the policy data -- the resend-after k\n   435\t            (emit! link v)\n   436\t\n   437\t            :else\n   438\t            (do (swap! link assoc-in\n   439\t                       [:filed id] {:req req :ans v :reflection refl})\n   440\t                (install-more! link v))))))))\n   441\t\n   442\t\n   443\t(defn- channel-loss!\n   444\t  \"The channel reader answered end: the channel is gone. The link\n   445\t   abandons its outstanding ids, reporting each abandoned append! on\n   446\t   the event writer as append-unknown; filed answers are kept and\n   447\t   still returned; reattachment is the caller's policy.\"\n   448\t  [link]\n   449\t  (doseq [[id entry] (:outstanding @link)]\n   450\t    (when (= :dao.stream/append! (:dao.stream.remote/op (:req entry)))\n   451\t      (emit! link {:dao.stream.remote/event\n   452\t                   :dao.stream.remote/append-unknown\n   453\t                   :dao.stream.remote/id id}))\n   454\t    (swap! (:reflection entry) update :ids disj id))\n   455\t  (swap! link assoc :outstanding {} :channel-gone? true))\n   456\t\n   457\t\n   458\t(defn- retry-pending!\n   459\t  \"One more try of each probe the writer has refused, once per drain,\n   460\t   until a send is accepted; the accepted send is registered as the\n   461\t   outstanding probe and the normal filing path confirms it.\"\n   462\t  [link]\n   463\t  (doseq [[_ e] (:pending @link)]\n   464\t    (send-request! link (:reflection e) (:req e))))\n   465\t\n   130\t      